  "_notes": [
    "SET UP BY: a real category-'Q' request minted through the same AddDocument path the till uses, then open · attachCustomer. The request's store is NOT the agent's, so the link's store copy is a real plant move.",
    "\uD83D\uDEA9 header.plantSource is `fromLinkedRequest`, the FIFTH value, and it does NOT shut 871's gate: the PHARMACIST who raised the request chose that store and the request document is the evidence. It is its own value and not a re-use of chosenForPickup — collapsing them would lose the distinction 871 was built to keep, a store the AGENT picked versus one a DOCUMENT supplied.",
    "\uD83D\uDEA9 linkRequest is ONE compound act behind ONE requestId: refuse unless the basket is EMPTY (LINES_EXIST), stamp, copy the store, fork on TMRA to pickup + online, prefill sourceReference only when empty, and copy the lines through addItem's own guardrails. The link STANDS regardless of how many lines landed.",
    "\uD83D\uDEA9 The read is scoped by LOYALTY ID and refuses NO_CUSTOMER_ATTACHED before it queries. That is a safety property: GetSalesRequestList's filter is `@CustomerId IS NULL OR …`, so an unscoped call lists the whole estate. Not by PHONE, because one number is a household and a relative's request must not be offerable.",
    "⚠ The reason arrives with its description resolved SERVER-side off the SREQ group (057) — the agent must never read a bare `TMRA`, and the console may not call SdDocument/ReasonsByGroup, which its CallCenterWeb grant does not cover.",
    "⚠ NO MONEY on customerRequests[] — the request is unpriced, so there is no price to carry and none may be invented.",
    "\uD83D\uDEA9 unlinkRequest is a FULL undo, forced by §4.1 rather than chosen: the invariant `linkable ⇔ empty basket` has to survive an unlink. WPF's CancelRequestLink drops the stamp alone, correctly — it copies no items, so it never had this problem.",
    "NOT captured here, and unreachable without a second actor: REQUEST_ALREADY_CONVERTED, the submit's mapping of 055c's one-shot guard for a request converted between the link and the submit. It is pinned as a unit in Data.Tests/CallCenterWeb/CallCenterLinkedRequestTests."
  ]
}
